data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** A guide RNA directs Cas9 to a specific DNA site, where it makes a cut [1]. Programmable molecules create double-strand breaks that allow DNA to be inserted, deleted, modified, or replaced [3].\n\n- **Natural origin:** CRISPR comes from a bacterial antiviral defense system [1]. In prokaryotes, CRISPR sequences derive from phage DNA and help detect and destroy similar phages during later infections [2].\n\n- **Applications, with limits:** Reports describe work aimed at treating many diseases [4] and eliminating HIV in cell culture [5]. The HIV result applies only to cell culture, not to patients."}

